 "summary_en": "On the HUS lung cancer pathway page, the referral is made by a doctor in primary care after a suspicious chest X-ray. The HUS page for the Kymenlaakso central hospital X-ray unit offers walk-in X-rays but says nothing about same-day reports or immediate CT, and a further search found no pilot. A randomised trial in London (Thorax 2023) found that reading primary-care chest X-rays straight away cut the median time to lung cancer diagnosis from 63 to 32 days.",
 "unanswered_en": "I found no HUS or Kymenhva page on how fast chest X-rays are reported, on CT in the same week, or on radiology making the referral itself.",
